FILE     fbg28.nc (from line 1)
DIALECT  series a 0 6 10 15 16 0i 30i (nothing series-specific used)
NOTE     G0 with Z and X/Y: the DX32 moves Z first up or last down, FANUC all at once
NOTE     G43/G49 left out: the DX32 applies the tool length of the tool in the spindle from its table (TENTATIVE)
NOTE     T without M6 left out: the DX32 takes T in the M6 block
NOTE     -ftool 1: T1 must be in the spindle when the program starts
NOTE     G28 X/Y go to the intermediate point only (-g28xy stay): the DX32 has no X/Y reference return; check the program is safe there
NOTE     G28 Z written as M25, the DX32 quill home (TENTATIVE: check that it goes where FANUC's reference point is) (-g28)
NOTE     the output needs BOSS 4-7 compatibility mode off
WROTE    fbwg28.txt
CHECK    dxsim reads fbwg28.txt cleanly and reaches all 10 FANUC end points in order
RESULT   ok
